  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Relations Q3 - How relations and functions connect</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Which statement correctly describes the connection between relations and functions?</p>
<div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A <strong>relation</strong> is any rule or set of ordered pairs linking elements of one set to elements of another. A <strong>function</strong> is a relation with an extra condition: every input is linked to exactly one output.</p>
<p>Because a function is a relation that satisfies an extra condition, every function is a relation. The reverse is false: a relation in which one input has several outputs is not a function.</p>
<p>Option A is false, because one-to-many and many-to-many relations are not functions.</p>
<p>Options C and D are false, because both one-to-one and many-to-one relations are functions. Neither type on its own covers all functions.</p>
<p>The correct answer is B.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
